1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
This is the clay room, where every
class starts on a Tuesday evening.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,500
The wheels along the wall are shared,
so please wipe your seat when you leave.

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,800
Shelves by the window hold the work
that is drying before its first firing.

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:13,000
Each shelf is labelled with a name,
and a full shelf holds about
40
small bowls.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,400
The kiln sits in the back room, and
only the instructors may load it.

6
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:19,700
Glazes are mixed on Fridays, so ask
early if you want a particular color.

7
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:23,000
There is a sink with a trap for clay
water, and the bucket beside it is
for scraps only.

8
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,300
Aprons hang on the hooks by the door,
and the tea kettle is always on.

9
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:29,500
That is the whole tour, so pick a
wheel and we will begin.
